  sql_0018,sql,"The SQLite database 'Database for tasks.sqlite3' in the current directory has tables: CATEGORY(WARE, CLASS) - which category (CLASS) a ware belongs to (a ware may belong to several categories); MANUFACTURER(BILL_ID, COMPANY) - bills of materials and the companies owning them; MATERIAL(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT) - materials used by a bill; PRODUCT(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT, PRICE) - wares produced by a bill, with amount and price. A bill may produce several wares. Show the production chains of task 2.8 in terms of wares (3 wares per chain): the first bill uses ware w1 and produces ware w2, the second bill uses w2 and produces w3; both bills belong to the same company. Each chain is unique. Write one chain per line as company;w1;w2;w3. Sort by company name first, then by the middle ware w2, then by w1, then by w3. Compute the answer with bash (sqlite3 and/or python3). Work only inside the current directory. When you are done, write ONLY the final answer to the file answer.txt in the current directory (for example with bash: echo 42 > answer.txt).",5,"A-Mark Precious Metals;Charcoal;Drinking water;Meat cow\nA-Mark Precious Metals;Water;Drinking water;Meat cow\nARMOUR Residential REIT;Meat cow;Meat;Steak\nAlbany Molecular Research;Charcoal;Drinking water;Meat\nAlbany Molecular Research;Charcoal;Drinking water;Water\nAlbany Molecular Research;Water;Drinking water;Meat\nAlbany Molecular Research;Water;Drinking water;Water\nAlbany Molecular Research;Charcoal;Water;Drinking water\nAlbany Molecular Research;Crude oil;Water;Drinking water\nAlbany Molecular Research;Drinking water;Water;Drinking water\nAltera Corporation;Wood;Charcoal;Drinking water\nArch Capital Group Ltd.;Wood;Charcoal;Steak\nAsanko Gold Inc.;Charcoal;Drinking water;Meat cow\nAsanko Gold Inc.;Water;Drinking water;Meat cow\nAssured Guaranty Ltd.;Charcoal;Water;Paper\nAssured Guaranty Ltd.;Crude oil;Water;Paper\nAssured Guaranty Ltd.;Drinking water;Water;Paper\nBioAmber Inc.;Charcoal;Drinking water;Mea