  sql_0019,sql,"The SQLite database 'Database for tasks.sqlite3' in the current directory has tables: CATEGORY(WARE, CLASS) - which category (CLASS) a ware belongs to (a ware may belong to several categories); MANUFACTURER(BILL_ID, COMPANY) - bills of materials and the companies owning them; MATERIAL(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT) - materials used by a bill; PRODUCT(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT, PRICE) - wares produced by a bill, with amount and price. A bill may produce several wares. Get all the unique wares in the alphabetic order with the minimal and maximal prices for each. Write one row per line as ware;min;max, both prices rounded to one decimal point. Compute the answer with bash (sqlite3 and/or python3). Work only inside the current directory. When you are done, write ONLY the final answer to the file answer.txt in the current directory (for example with bash: echo 42 > answer.txt).",4,"Charcoal;5.0;9.9\nCrude oil;14.1;25.8\nDrinking water;3.0;4.9\nGold;1000.3;1299.7\nGold ore;5.4;14.8\nGrain;4.0;7.9\nLeather;20.1;29.9\nMeat;4.0;14.9\nMeat cow;100.0;149.5\nPaper;4.0;6.9\nSalt;2.0;3.9\nSteak;30.0;44.9\nWater;1.0;1.9\nWood;5.0;14.9",exact_str
  sql_0020,sql,"The SQLite database 'Database for tasks.sqlite3' in the current directory has tables: CATEGORY(WARE, CLASS) - which category (CLASS) a ware belongs to (a ware may belong to several categories); MANUFACTURER(BILL_ID, COMPANY) - bills of materials and the companies owning them; MATERIAL(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT) - materials used by a bill; PRODUCT(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT, PRICE) - wares produced by a bill, with amount and price. A bill may produce several wares. Show top 3 wares with the most difference between minimal and maximal prices. Write exactly 3 rows as ware;diff, where diff is (max price - min price) rounded to one decimal point. Sort by diff descending; ties broken by ware name in alphabetical order. Compute the answer with bash (sqlite3 and/or python3). Work only inside the current directory. When you are done, write ONLY the final answer to the file answer.txt in the current directory (for example with bash: echo 42 > answer.txt).",4,"Gold;299.4\nMeat cow;49.5\nSteak;14.9",exact_str
  sql_0021,sql,"The SQLite database 'Database for tasks.sqlite3' in the current directory has tables: CATEGORY(WARE, CLASS) - which category (CLASS) a ware belongs to (a ware may belong to several categories); MANUFACTURER(BILL_ID, COMPANY) - bills of materials and the companies owning them; MATERIAL(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT) - materials used by a bill; PRODUCT(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT, PRICE) - wares produced by a bill, with amount and price. A bill may produce several wares. Show top 3 companies producing the largest number of different products. Write exactly 3 rows as company;count. Sort by count descending; ties broken by company name in alphabetical order. Compute the answer with bash (sqlite3 and/or python3). Work only inside the current directory. When you are done, write ONLY the final answer to the file answer.txt in the current directory (for example with bash: echo 42 > answer.txt).",2,"Juniper Networks;7\nRediff.com India Limited;7\nSimon Property Group;7",exact_str
  sql_0022,sql,"The SQLite database 'Database for tasks.sqlite3' in the current directory has tables: CATEGORY(WARE, CLASS) - which category (CLASS) a ware belongs to (a ware may belong to several categories); MANUFACTURER(BILL_ID, COMPANY) - bills of materials and the companies owning them; MATERIAL(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT) - materials used by a bill; PRODUCT(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT, PRICE) - wares produced by a bill, with amount and price. A bill may produce several wares. Show the price of the most expensive ware for each category (the maximal price among all product records of the wares in the category). The result should be ordered by the category. Write one row per line as category;price, the price rounded to one decimal point. Compute the answer with bash (sqlite3 and/or python3). Work only inside the current directory. When you are done, write ONLY the final answer to the file answer.txt in the current directory (for example with bash: echo 42 > answer.txt).",2,"Chemicals;25.8\nFood;44.9\nFuel;25.8\nLivestock;149.5\nMineral;14.8\nRaw food;14.9\nRaw material;14.9\nReady food;44.9\nStuff;1299.7",exact_str
  sql_0023,sql,"The SQLite database 'Database for tasks.sqlite3' in the current directory has tables: CATEGORY(WARE, CLASS) - which category (CLASS) a ware belongs to (a ware may belong to several categories); MANUFACTURER(BILL_ID, COMPANY) - bills of materials and the companies owning them; MATERIAL(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT) - materials used by a bill; PRODUCT(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT, PRICE) - wares produced by a bill, with amount and price. A bill may produce several wares. For each bill of materials show the company and lists of all the products and materials. The result must contain exactly one row per bill and be sorted by the company. Write one row per line as bill_id;company;products;materials. Each list is a string of values separated with comma (no spaces) with the values sorted alphabetically; an empty list is an empty string. Sort rows by company name first, then by bill_id. Compute the answer with bash (sqlite3 and/or python3). Work only inside the current directory. When you are done, write ONLY the final answer to the file answer.txt in the current directory (for example with bash: echo 42 > answer.txt).",5,"1895;1-800 FLOWERS.COM;Drinking water;Charcoal,Water\n65;3M Company;Water;\n168;3M Company;Leather,Meat;Meat cow\n1800;3M Company;Water;\n27;A-Mark Precious Metals;Meat cow;Drinking water,Grain\n73;A-Mark Precious Metals;Water;\n957;A-Mark Precious Metals;Steak;Charcoal,Meat,Salt\n1875;A-Mark Precious Metals;Drinking water;Charcoal,Water\n821;A. Schulman;Drinking water;Charcoal,Water\n1355;ADT Corporation;Grain;\n1442;ADT Corporation;Crude oil;Water\n1735;ADT Corporation;Crude oil;Water\n78;AEterna Zentaris Inc.;Grain;\n1293;AEterna Zentaris Inc.;Wood;\n842;AGCO Corporation;Gold;Gold ore\n1010;AGCO Corporation;Grain;\n1257;AGCO Corporation;Paper;Water,Wood\n1839;AGCO Corporation;Wood;\n803;AMERIPRISE FINANCIAL SERVICES;Wood;\n1775;AMERIPRISE FINANCIAL SERVICES;Water;\n177;AMERISAFE;Grain;\n396;AMERISAFE;Charcoal;Wood\n1851;AMERISAFE;Wood;\n1961;AMERISAF