  sql_0027,sql,"The SQLite database 'Database for tasks.sqlite3' in the current directory has tables: CATEGORY(WARE, CLASS) - which category (CLASS) a ware belongs to (a ware may belong to several categories); MANUFACTURER(BILL_ID, COMPANY) - bills of materials and the companies owning them; MATERIAL(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT) - materials used by a bill; PRODUCT(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT, PRICE) - wares produced by a bill, with amount and price. A bill may produce several wares. For each company get the list of all the categories of materials used and the list of categories of products. The result must contain exactly one row per company and each list must contain only the unique entries. Write one row per line as company;material_categories;product_categories. Each list is a string of values separated with comma (no spaces), sorted alphabetically; an empty list is an empty string. Sort rows by company name. Compute the answer with bash (sqlite3 and/or python3). Work only inside the current directory. When you are done, write ONLY the final answer to the file answer.txt in the current directory (for example with bash: echo 42 > answer.txt).",2,"1-800 FLOWERS.COM;Chemicals,Fuel,Mineral;Food,Ready food\n3M Company;Livestock;Food,Mineral,Raw food,Stuff\nA-Mark Precious Metals;Chemicals,Food,Fuel,Mineral,Raw food,Ready food;Food,Livestock,Mineral,Ready food\nA. Schulman;Chemicals,Fuel,Mineral;Food,Ready food\nADT Corporation;Mineral;Chemicals,Food,Fuel,Raw food\nAEterna Zentaris Inc.;;Food,Raw food,Raw material\nAGCO Corporation;Mineral,Raw material;Food,Raw food,Raw material,Stuff\nAMERIPRISE FINANCIAL SERVICES;;Mineral,Raw material\nAMERISAFE;Mineral,Raw material;Chemicals,Food,Fuel,Raw food,Raw material,Stuff\nANI Pharmaceuticals;Mineral;Chemicals,Fuel,Stuff\nARMOUR Residential REIT;Chemicals,Food,Fuel,Livestock,Mineral,Raw food,Raw material;Food,Raw food,Raw material,Ready food,Stuff\nATRION Corporation;;Food,Mineral,Raw food\nAbbVie Inc.;Mineral,Raw material;Stuff\nAbbott 