  sql_0029,sql,"The SQLite database 'Database for tasks.sqlite3' in the current directory has tables: CATEGORY(WARE, CLASS) - which category (CLASS) a ware belongs to (a ware may belong to several categories); MANUFACTURER(BILL_ID, COMPANY) - bills of materials and the companies owning them; MATERIAL(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT) - materials used by a bill; PRODUCT(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT, PRICE) - wares produced by a bill, with amount and price. A bill may produce several wares. Show the product with the largest average price over the market (the average is taken over all product records of the ware; if several wares tie, take the alphabetically first one). Write the single ware name. Compute the answer with bash (sqlite3 and/or python3). Work only inside the current directory. When you are done, write ONLY the final answer to the file answer.txt in the current directory (for example with bash: echo 42 > answer.txt).",2,Gold,exact_str
  sql_0030,sql,"The SQLite database 'Database for tasks.sqlite3' in the current directory has tables: CATEGORY(WARE, CLASS) - which category (CLASS) a ware belongs to (a ware may belong to several categories); MANUFACTURER(BILL_ID, COMPANY) - bills of materials and the companies owning them; MATERIAL(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT) - materials used by a bill; PRODUCT(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT, PRICE) - wares produced by a bill, with amount and price. A bill may produce several wares. Show one sample ware from each category (the alphabetically first ware of the category). Write one row per line as category;ware, sorted by category name. Compute the answer with bash (sqlite3 and/or python3). Work only inside the current directory. When you are done, write ONLY the final answer to the file answer.txt in the current directory (for example with bash: echo 42 > answer.txt).",3,"Chemicals;Charcoal\nFood;Drinking water\nFuel;Charcoal\nLivestock;Meat cow\nMineral;Gold ore\nRaw food;Grain\nRaw material;Wood\nReady food;Drinking water\nStuff;Gold",exact_str
  sql_0031,sql,"The SQLite database 'Database for tasks.sqlite3' in the current directory has tables: CATEGORY(WARE, CLASS) - which category (CLASS) a ware belongs to (a ware may belong to several categories); MANUFACTURER(BILL_ID, COMPANY) - bills of materials and the companies owning them; MATERIAL(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT) - materials used by a bill; PRODUCT(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT, PRICE) - wares produced by a bill, with amount and price. A bill may produce several wares. Show the most expensive ware in each category and its price. The most expensive ware is the ware with the maximal price among all product records of the wares in the category; if several wares tie, take the alphabetically first one. Write one row per line as category;ware;price, the price rounded to one decimal point, sorted by category name. Compute the answer with bash (sqlite3 and/or python3). Work only inside the current directory. When you are done, write ONLY the final answer to the file answer.txt in the current directory (for example with bash: echo 42 > answer.txt).",1,"Chemicals;Crude oil;25.8\nFood;Steak;44.9\nFuel;Crude oil;25.8\nLivestock;Meat cow;149.5\nMineral;Gold ore;14.8\nRaw food;Meat;14.9\nRaw material;Wood;14.9\nReady food;Steak;44.9\nStuff;Gold;1299.7",exact_str
  sql_0032,sql,"The SQLite database 'Database for tasks.sqlite3' in the current directory has tables: CATEGORY(WARE, CLASS) - which category (CLASS) a ware belongs to (a ware may belong to several categories); MANUFACTURER(BILL_ID, COMPANY) - bills of materials and the companies owning them; MATERIAL(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT) - materials used by a bill; PRODUCT(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT, PRICE) - wares produced by a bill, with amount and price. A bill may produce several wares. Show the list of all the 'greedy' companies: companies selling all the wares they produce with prices at least 20% higher than the average price of this ware on the market (the average over all product records of the ware; every price the company has for every ware it produces must be at least 20% above that average). Write one company name per line, sorted alphabetically. Compute the answer with bash (sqlite3 and/or python3). Work only inside the current directory. When you are done, write ONLY the final answer to the file answer.txt in the current directory (for example with bash: echo 42 > answer.txt).",1,"AMERIPRISE FINANCIAL SERVICES\nAcme United Corporation.\nAllegion plc\nAmeresco\nAshland Inc.\nAvnet\nB/E Aerospace\nBank of the Ozarks\nBitauto Holdings Limited\nBlucora\nCardinal Financial Corporation\nCareer Education Corporation\nCascade Bancorp\nCeragon Networks Ltd.\nCheetah Mobile Inc.\nDataram Corporation\nEastern Virginia Bankshares\nElectronics for Imaging\nHDFC Bank Limited\nHanesbrands Inc.\nIcahn Enterprises L.P.\nJabil Circuit\nLifePoint Health\nMFRI\nMarin Software Incorporated\nMarineMax\nMazor Robotics Ltd.\nMetabolix\nMetro Bancorp\nMonro Muffler Brake\nNCR Corporation\nNortheast Community Bancorp\nOtter Tail Corporation\nParke Bancorp\nParkway Properties\nPreferred Apartment Communities\nRuby Tuesday\nSPAR Group\nSanchez Production Partners LP\nSeres Therapeutics\nSouthern First Bancshares\nSouthwestern Energy Company\nStrategic Hotels & Resorts Inc\nTSR\nTasman Metals Ltd\nTeekay Offshore Partners L.P.\nUnique Fabricating\nVBI Vaccines Inc.\nWGL Holdings Inc\nWSI Industries Inc.\nvoxeljet AG",exact_str
  sql_0033,sql,"The SQLite database 'Database for tasks.sqlite3' in the current directory has tables: CATEGORY(WARE, CLASS) - which category (CLASS) a ware belongs to (a ware may belong to several categories); MANUFACTURER(BILL_ID, COMPANY) - bills of materials and the companies owning them; MATERIAL(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT) - materials used by a bill; PRODUCT(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT, PRICE) - wares produced by a bill, with amount and price. A bill may produce several wares. Show the companies that produce all the wares from any category. The result should contain the company and the category and be sorted by the category, enriched with the column of all the wares in the given category that the given company is actually producing. Write one row per line as company;category;wares, where wares is a comma-separated list (no spaces) of wares sorted alphabetically. Sort rows by category name first, then by company name. Compute the answer with bash (sqlite3 and/or python3). Work only inside the current directory. When you are done, write ONLY the final answer to the file answer.txt in the current directory (for example with bash: echo 42 > answer.txt).",3,"Apple Inc.;Chemicals;Charcoal,Crude oil\nCSP Inc.;Chemicals;Charcoal,Crude oil\nCanadian Natural Resources Limited;Chemicals;Charcoal,Crude oil\nCastle Brands;Chemicals;Charcoal,Crude oil\nErickson Incorporated;Chemicals;Charcoal,Crude oil\nGlycoMimetics;Chemicals;Charcoal,Crude oil\nIncome Opportunity Realty Investors;Chemicals;Charcoal,Crude oil\nJuniper Networks;Chemicals;Charcoal,Crude oil\nLexington Realty Trust;Chemicals;Charcoal,Crude oil\nMannKind Corporation;Chemicals;Charcoal,Crude oil\nThe Spectranetics Corporation;Chemicals;Charcoal,Crude oil\nTimken Steel Corporation;Chemicals;Charcoal,Crude oil\nUnited Fire Group;Chemicals;Charcoal,Crude oil\nApple Inc.;Fuel;Charcoal,Crude oil\nCSP Inc.;Fuel;Charcoal,Crude oil\nCanadian Natural Resources Limited;Fuel;Charcoal,Crude oil\nCastle Brands;Fuel;Charcoal,Crude oil\n