  sql_0034,sql,"The SQLite database 'Database for tasks.sqlite3' in the current directory has tables: CATEGORY(WARE, CLASS) - which category (CLASS) a ware belongs to (a ware may belong to several categories); MANUFACTURER(BILL_ID, COMPANY) - bills of materials and the companies owning them; MATERIAL(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT) - materials used by a bill; PRODUCT(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT, PRICE) - wares produced by a bill, with amount and price. A bill may produce several wares. For each bill of materials show the company, all the materials, all the products and the total price of all the products considering their amounts (sum of amount*price over the products of the bill). There must be exactly one row per bill and the result must be ordered by the company. Write one row per line as bill_id;company;materials;products;total. The lists are comma-separated (no spaces) values sorted alphabetically; an empty list is an empty string. The total is rounded to one decimal point. Sort rows by company name first, then by bill_id. Compute the answer with bash (sqlite3 and/or python3). Work only inside the current directory. When you are done, write ONLY the final answer to the file answer.txt in the current directory (for example with bash: echo 42 > answer.txt).",4,"1895;1-800 FLOWERS.COM;Charcoal,Water;Drinking water;27.0\n65;3M Company;;Water;1.2\n168;3M Company;Meat cow;Leather,Meat;281.1\n1800;3M Company;;Water;1.3\n27;A-Mark Precious Metals;Drinking water,Grain;Meat cow;221.2\n73;A-Mark Precious Metals;;Water;1.7\n957;A-Mark Precious Metals;Charcoal,Meat,Salt;Steak;84.6\n1875;A-Mark Precious Metals;Charcoal,Water;Drinking water;32.8\n821;A. Schulman;Charcoal,Water;Drinking water;30.6\n1355;ADT Corporation;;Grain;7.6\n1442;ADT Corporation;Water;Crude oil;66.3\n1735;ADT Corporation;Water;Crude oil;96.0\n78;AEterna Zentaris Inc.;;Grain;5.5\n1293;AEterna Zentaris Inc.;;Wood;6.6\n842;AGCO Corporation;Gold ore;Gold;5128.0\n1010;AGCO Corporation;;Grain;4.7\n1257;AGCO Corporation;Water